stateDiagram-v2
    state "issued (status_id 10)" as issued
    state "attached (status_id 20)" as attached
    state "Base confirmed (status_id 30)" as confirmed
    state "redeemed (status_id 40)" as redeemed
    state "retired (status_id 90)" as retired
    state "switched (status_id 91)" as switched

    [*] --> issued: parent + binding transaction
    issued --> attached: attach_auth_session!
    issued --> retired: retire! / expiry or restart
    attached --> confirmed: confirm_base! / browser nonce proof
    attached --> retired: retire! / expiry or restart
    confirmed --> redeemed: redeem! / admitted rotated session
    confirmed --> retired: retire! / expiry or restart
    redeemed --> switched: switch! / canceled first-page ceremony
    redeemed --> [*]: retained accepted admission
    retired --> [*]: retained terminal fact
    switched --> [*]: retained switched fact

    note right of issued
      operator_auth_admission_binding_statuses is an id-only reference table.
      status_id is NOT NULL and is the lifecycle authority.
      Proof timestamps and session ids remain immutable facts.
      Active parent+purpose uniqueness covers status ids 10, 20, 30.
      Expiry is a time condition; purge first retires active rows.
      ORG public Switch remains unavailable under the current product contract.
    end note

    note right of attached
      An attached reference is usable only when the current host-only auth_sid
      resolves to the exact active Auth continuity row. A mismatch returns 409
      before redirect, mutation, or Auth-cookie/DBSC issuance.
    end note

    note right of confirmed
      Auth entry redemption requires Sec-Fetch-Mode: navigate and
      Sec-Fetch-Dest: document. Missing or other metadata and HEAD are refused
      before the binding or Auth continuity changes.
    end note

    note right of redeemed
      The shared writer accepts Switch only when the encrypted handoff names
      this exact admitted Auth session and its browser/token proof matches.
      The old row becomes status 91 in the same Ticket transaction that
      creates a replacement. Switched rows retain proof and accept no result.
    end note

    note right of retired
      The purger waits for parent, binding and referenced Auth session
      retention boundaries, then deletes Flow children before the binding.
      After the last binding reference is removed, it may delete an expired
      Auth session once its expiry or terminal event reaches retention. The
      collector does not change Auth session status or delete principals.
    end note
